    "turn_text": "and foreign aid package this week. You might recall that the Senate had sent over a bipartisan bill that was negotiated over the course of months. And then Speaker Johnson refused to bring up that Senate bill. but is breaking it up into various pieces, you know, for potentially five different bills that will be voting on well into the weekend. So the the corners of that are being negotiated and Marjorie Taylor Greene is threatening to bring another motion to vacate the chair of the speaker as a result. So that's kind of the chaos on the main stage. But you guys know, one of the things I talk a lot about is while there is absolute chaos and division in Washington, all of that is very real. I try to push past that and focus on bipartisan solutions and the things that matter to West Michigan. So even in the midst of all this chaos today, really happy to report that I got my bipartisan bill focusing on access to capital for small businesses passed unanimously out of the small business committee today. And we expect that to come to the house floor during small business week. and hopefully get that, get that past. So all our small business owners tuning in, you know that access to capital is one of the, you know, the most important issues that small businesses can deal with. So, you know, my capital for all bill is making sure that we are getting that capital into rural and low income communities in particular. I'm really excited about it. We're just recently focused on delivering for the people of West Michigan on that issue.",
