    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, we hope so. You guys know I've been working on immigration for close to 20 years. And I am an original co-sponsor of I-partisan immigration reform bill that would send $10 billion to the southern border to help us enforce our immigration laws, help keep our southern border safe. and secure. This is not a game. We have seen the impact of failed immigrant policies back home and it's impacting our communities in real ways. You know, a couple months ago, I had the opportunity to visit the southern border. And even though I've been working on this issue for so long, I was I was shocked and horrified by what I saw, you know, just an absolute overwhelming situation. There are just two few individuals presenting themselves at the southern border every single day that the officers can inspect and you know there this notion that we can somehow just completely shut down the border. is nonsense. We have so many goods and services that travel across the southern border legally,",
